-- Writing (12 prompt)

You want next Friday off for a family event. Write a short email to your manager, Mr. Diallo. Say which day you need off and why. (30–50 words)', 'A strong response uses simple present/future forms and clearly states the date and reason.'),
  ('writing', 'A1', 'prompt', 'general', 'Welcome Note for a New Colleague

A new team member, Ana, starts on Monday. Write a short welcome note. Say hello, tell her your name, and say you are happy she is joining the team. (30–50 words)', 'A strong response greets warmly, introduces the writer, and uses simple friendly vocabulary correctly.'),
  ('writing', 'A2', 'prompt', 'email', 'Office Move Announcement

Your office is moving to a new building on 5th Street starting next month. Write a short email to staff. Give the new address, the start date, and tell them where to park. (50–80 words)', 'A strong response gives clear factual details (address, date, instructions) in simple, well-organized sentences.'),
  ('writing', 'A2', 'prompt', 'general', 'Instructions for Covering the Front Desk

Your colleague Tom is covering the front desk while you are at lunch. Write simple instructions for him: how to greet visitors, where the sign-in sheet is, and what to do if the phone rings. (50–80 words)', 'A strong response gives clear, ordered instructions using simple imperative forms.'),
  ('writing', 'B1', 'prompt', 'email', 'Replying to a Job Application Question

A candidate named Priya emailed asking whether the Marketing Assistant position is still open and when interviews will start. Write a reply confirming the role is open, giving an approximate interview date, and telling her what documents to send. (80–120 words)', 'A strong response answers all three questions clearly and uses polite, professional email phrases.'),
  ('writing', 'B1', 'prompt', 'general', 'Summarizing Meeting Notes

You attended a team meeting where it was decided to launch the new website in September, assign Marco to lead design, and hold weekly check-ins on Mondays. Write a short summary of these notes to share with a colleague who missed the meeting. (80–120 words)', 'A strong response organizes the key decisions logically and reports them accurately in past/reported forms.'),
  ('writing', 'B2', 'prompt', 'email', 'Project Status Update

Write an email to your project sponsor updating them on the CRM migration project. Explain that data migration is 70% complete, testing has revealed two minor bugs being fixed this week, and the go-live date remains on track for August 15th. (120–160 words)', 'A strong response structures the update logically (progress, issues, timeline) with appropriate business vocabulary and reasoning.'),
  ('writing', 'B2', 'prompt', 'customer_service', 'Handling a Subscription Cancellation Request

A customer, Mr. Hendricks, emails asking to cancel his premium subscription because he feels it is too expensive. Reply confirming you can process the cancellation, explain what happens to his data and access, and mention a lower-cost plan he might consider instead. (120–160 words)', 'A strong response balances customer service tone with clear procedural explanation and a tactful alternative offer.'),
  ('writing', 'C1', 'prompt', 'email', 'Explaining a Policy Change

Your company is changing its remote-work policy so employees must now be in the office three days a week instead of two, starting next quarter. Write an email to your team explaining the reasoning behind the change, acknowledging it may be unwelcome, and outlining how flexibility will still be offered. (150–200 words)', 'A strong response explains reasoning persuasively, shows empathy for a negative reaction, and maintains a measured professional tone.'),
  ('writing', 'C1', 'prompt', 'general', 'Declining a Meeting Invitation Politely

A senior colleague, Ms. Okafor, has invited you to a strategy meeting that clashes with an existing client commitment you cannot move. Write a message declining the invitation, explaining the conflict without sounding dismissive, and proposing a way to stay informed or contribute asynchronously. (150–200 words)', 'A strong response declines gracefully while preserving the relationship, using hedging language and a constructive alternative.'),
  ('writing', 'C2', 'prompt', 'negotiation', 'Negotiating a Vendor Price Increase

Your long-standing office supplies vendor has notified you of a 15% price increase, citing rising raw material costs. Write an email negotiating this increase: acknowledge their cost pressures, present your case for a smaller increase or phased implementation based on your multi-year relationship, and propose next steps for discussion. (180–250 words)', 'A strong response demonstrates sophisticated negotiation tactics, balancing firmness and diplomacy while building a reasoned counter-argument.'),
  ('writing', 'C2', 'prompt', 'general', 'Following Up After a Networking Event

You met Dr. Elena Vasquez, a potential industry partner, at a conference last week and had a promising conversation about a possible collaboration. Write a follow-up message that reestablishes rapport, subtly reminds her of the specifics you discussed, and proposes a concrete next step without appearing overly eager. (180–250 words)', 'A strong response demonstrates nuanced relationship-building, calibrated tone, and persuasive yet understated professional writing.');

